WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:03.750
. We have a new report out from Goldman Sachs.

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:06.120
The report is shocking.

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:12.910
A lot of people and I don't know why the report
says that if Biden wins and there is a blue

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:19.810
wave in the Senate, if there is a big picture,
blue wave led by Joe Biden defeating Donald

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:20.810
Trump.

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:25.870
Goldman Sachs says it would lead to a surge
in economic growth.

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:27.820
And I see people acting all my.

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:28.820
Oh, my.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:29.820
A Democrat.

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:31.789
It would be good for the economy, Bill.

00:00:31.789 --> 00:00:33.310
I'm so shocked.

00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:34.310
No.

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:38.720
If you've watched my show for a while, you
would already know why Democratic presidents

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:40.570
are better for the economy.

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:46.520
Goldman wrote in a note yesterday that Democratic
control of the presidency and of Congress

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:51.489
would raise the probability of a fiscal stimulus
package worth at least two trillion dollars.

00:00:51.489 --> 00:00:57.340
But it's not just that longer term spending
measures that Joe Biden wants, like infrastructure,

00:00:57.340 --> 00:01:04.830
climate, health care, education that boosts
economic growth prospects, according to Goldman

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:05.830
Sachs.

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:10.560
Assuming that the Federal Reserve doesn't
mess with interest rates until we get back

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:13.830
to full employment and inflation just above
two percent.

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:19.520
Goldman Sachs estimates that, quote, the net
effect of the Biden package would be a front

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:26.540
loaded increase, as well as a more backloaded
boost to core p.c inflation.

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:32.740
Now, Goldman is also being upfront that if
Biden is successful, for example, in raising

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:38.380
the corporate income tax rate from 21 to 28,
maybe that wouldn't be so good for markets

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:39.380
and for the economy.

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:42.210
There is debate there, but would that even
get passed?

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:44.890
It really depends on what happens in the Senate
now.

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:52.210
On the positive side, Goldman also says if
we get a blue wave in November, we will likely

00:01:52.210 --> 00:02:00.479
have easier U.S. fiscal policy or renew a
reduced risk of trade escalation and a firmer

00:02:00.479 --> 00:02:02.079
global growth outlook.

00:02:02.079 --> 00:02:06.299
We call it stability when Donald Trump is
gone.

00:02:06.299 --> 00:02:12.150
But none of this should surprise you because
the country does better economically under

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:13.910
Democratic presidents.

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:16.390
I talked about this 15 years ago.

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:18.420
I talked about it 10 years ago.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:20.370
I talked about it five years ago.

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:22.000
I talked about it in June.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:27.480
This is not about whether Democratic presidents
are left enough or really progressive or what.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:30.760
This is merely about looking at a totality
of indicators.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:35.380
When you have a Democratic president versus
a Republican president and it's better under

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:36.380
Democrats.

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:38.360
So why would it be any different under Joe
Biden?

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:39.820
Let's look at those metrics.

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:43.390
Typically, we would look at GDP growth.

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:46.060
Unemployment, stock market performance.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:50.000
Then there's other intangibles like respect
around the world, you can look at poverty,

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.700
inflation, different elements.

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:57.879
Stock market, average annualized return when
you have a Democratic president is fourteen

00:02:57.879 --> 00:02:59.489
point three percent.

00:02:59.489 --> 00:03:01.769
It is ten point eight percent under Republicans.

00:03:01.769 --> 00:03:05.490
The stock market does about 40 percent better
under Democratic presidents.

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:07.470
But that's not the economy.

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:11.830
What about GDP, gross domestic product through
2008?

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:18.400
Real GDP grew faster under Democratic administrations
than Republican four point one versus two

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:19.510
point seven.

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:24.860
If you were to extend those numbers to today,
Barack Obama had better GDP numbers than Donald

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:25.860
Trump.

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:31.150
So it remains GDP and stocks better with a
Democratic president.

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:33.599
What about income growth while under Democrats?

00:03:33.599 --> 00:03:39.050
Real median income over the last 50 years
grew at two point two percent per year under

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:40.620
Republicans only point six percent.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:43.750
So there you've got wages on the flip side.

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:51.190
Unemployment has been 18 percent higher under
Republican presidents since World War two

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:52.980
job creation.

00:03:52.980 --> 00:04:00.220
Democratic presidents have seen 24 million
more jobs created on their watch, with an

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:07.720
average of 78 percent more jobs created per
year of a Democratic administration than during

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:09.750
a Republican administration.

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:15.959
Bloomberg looked at U.S. job creation and
found that for the close to half century following

00:04:15.959 --> 00:04:18.469
the Kennedy administration.

00:04:18.469 --> 00:04:19.690
Democrats have created.

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:20.690
Wait for it.

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:25.199
Nearly twice as many private sector jobs as
Republicans.

00:04:25.199 --> 00:04:32.370
Even though Democrats have had the presidency
for five fewer years during that time, none

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:35.979
of this is new and none of this is news.

00:04:35.979 --> 00:04:37.949
This is the reality.

00:04:37.949 --> 00:04:46.639
And we see Republicans maintain almost a monopoly
on the reputation of being good for the economy.

00:04:46.639 --> 00:04:50.710
How many Republican governors have actually
destroyed state budgets?

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:52.569
Look at what happened in Kansas.

00:04:52.569 --> 00:04:57.560
But if you've been following the data, you
would know that this is merely a lie.

00:04:57.560 --> 00:05:03.589
And even on economy, Trump's numbers are worse
compared to Biden's than most Republicans.

00:05:03.589 --> 00:05:07.949
Again, there's this idea that Republicans
are better for the economy.

00:05:07.949 --> 00:05:08.949
They are not.

00:05:08.949 --> 00:05:12.589
When they say Republicans are good for the
economy, what they mean is Republicans will

00:05:12.589 --> 00:05:18.080
cut regulations and it will it will allow
companies to make money by polluting companies

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:22.800
to make money, by taking advantage of the
environment, taking advantage of employees.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:25.639
That lets the very rich get slightly richer.

00:05:25.639 --> 00:05:28.659
But it's not so good for the economy overall.

00:05:28.659 --> 00:05:33.139
When Republicans say we're good for the economy
because of small government, they mean we

00:05:33.139 --> 00:05:38.110
will cut education and we will cut welfare,
but we will keep writing blank checks to the

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:42.280
military budget will pay farmers to grow nothing
or to destroy crops.

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:46.659
And we will continue this failed idea of what
it means to run an economy.

00:05:46.659 --> 00:05:48.699
It is all horrible code.

00:05:48.699 --> 00:05:54.460
It's a moral code for really bad policies
that help the very rich but aren't so good

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:56.050
for everybody else.

00:05:56.050 --> 00:06:00.999
It's great that Goldman Sachs put out this
report, but it's not actually newsworthy because

00:06:00.999 --> 00:06:05.680
if you've been paying attention for the last
however many years, you would know that this

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:09.619
is a false notion that Republicans are great
for the economy.

00:06:09.619 --> 00:06:13.979
We'll have some of the data I mentioned today
on our Instagram page.

00:06:13.979 --> 00:06:18.319
OK, so make sure you're following us on Instagram
at David Pakman show.

00:06:18.319 --> 00:06:22.460
And while you're there, follow me on Instagram
for a break from politics.

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:24.979
It's Poppy's books.

00:06:24.979 --> 00:06:25.979
And what else?

00:06:25.979 --> 00:06:28.759
I don't know a lot of that on my Instagram.

